# CSS utilities first

Before writing new SCSS or inventing class names, check the **full catalog**:

**[apps/web-giddh/src/assets/styles/CSS_UTILITIES.md](apps/web-giddh/src/assets/styles/CSS_UTILITIES.md)**

That file lists every utility from:
- `utilities/_other.scss`
- `utilities/_text.scss` (mixin-generated)
- `base/_typography.scss`
- `themes/_theme-base-classes.scss`
- `pages/_dialog.scss`
- Bootstrap (`vendors/_boostrap.css`)

## Do

- Reuse layout: `d-flex`, `flex-column`, `align-items-*`, `justify-content-*`, `column-gap-*`, `row-gap-*`, Bootstrap `m-*` / `p-*`
- Reuse color: `text-primary`, `text-light`, `text-orange`, `theme-primary-light`, vars like `--border-color`, `--color-green`
- Reuse type: `font-size-12`, `font-weight-semibold`, `line-height-*`
- Reuse dialogs: `aside-dialog-wrapper`, `dialog-header`, `dialog-body`
- Keep feature-only styles in the **component `.scss`**

## Don't

- Do not add one-off/feature styles to `_other.scss`
- Do not hardcode hex when a theme variable exists
- Do not confuse `.w-100` (100%) with `.width-100` / `.w100` (100px)
- Prefer `.pointer-events-none` over misspelled `.pointer-event-none`
